# What never reaches the image build's context.
#
# Kept deliberately short and additive rather than an allow-list: the build
# embeds `internal/git/GIT_FLOOR` into the binary for gate 7, and an exclusion
# that swept it out would produce an image whose floor is whatever the last
# compile happened to see. Seam 2 builds this Dockerfile and runs the gate, so
# that mistake fails the suite rather than shipping.

# The git directory is the largest thing here and the build reads none of it —
# the version is stamped by --build-arg, never derived from a checkout.
.git
.gitignore

# CI, the AFK sandbox and its node tooling: none of it is shipped, and nothing
# in the image depends on it.
.github
.sandcastle
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json

# Documentation, which the image does not carry. LICENSE is not here: the image
# redistributes Apache-2.0 work and carries the licence it does so under.
docs
README.md
CONTEXT.md

# Build output from a local `go build`, which would otherwise be copied in and
# then overwritten by the builder's own.
/obsync
/bin
/dist
*.test
coverage.out
